Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.03,0:00:19.46,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um, where are we going?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.46,0:00:21.09,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,To Tilty's place.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.37,0:00:25.68,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Tilty... You mean the eldest \Ndaughter of Marquess Claret?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.00,0:00:26.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yep.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.94,0:00:33.27,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I seem to recall that her inhumane \Nnature has caused repeated problems,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.27,0:00:35.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,and that she's been locked up \Nin a separate building...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.59,0:00:38.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yep. That's pretty much right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.44,0:00:45.95,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Lady Tilty isn't, um... dangerous, is she?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.47,0:00:49.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah. She's super dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.85,0:00:54.06,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,She is certainly unusual.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.06,0:00:57.21,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,She is the princess's \Nresearch partner, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.92,0:01:01.87,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,In other words, she's the \Nsame type as the princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.50,0:02:42.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:02:33.50,0:02:42.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.50,0:02:42.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.79,0:03:01.81,Default,Maid,0,0,0,,My lady, I've brought visitors for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.62,0:03:04.05,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Let them in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.66,0:03:14.27,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,It's been a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.44,0:03:17.94,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sure has!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.94,0:03:21.13,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,And is that the beloved \Ndaughter of Duke Magenta?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.63,0:03:24.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah! She's my cute, sweet assistant!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.21,0:03:26.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,My name is Euphyllia Magenta.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.83,0:03:29.40,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's a pleasure to meet you, Lady Claret.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.40,0:03:32.90,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Call me Tilty. I hate formalities.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.90,0:03:35.83,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Your rank's higher than mine, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.23,0:03:37.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.64,0:03:42.23,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So why did you come meekly trailing along \Nwith her if you're just going to be silent?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.12,0:03:51.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I wanted to get your advice \Nregarding this dragon magicite.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.40,0:03:53.88,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Wow, so this is what \NI've heard so much about.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.88,0:03:58.45,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You want me to use this the next time \NI synthesize magic medicine, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.45,0:04:00.11,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Actually, nope!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.11,0:04:03.17,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I want to test out a new technique with it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.17,0:04:06.80,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You didn't come up with some \Nderanged idea again, did you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.80,0:04:08.42,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.63,0:04:12.85,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I was cursed by that dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.70,0:04:19.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Actually, it might be more correct to say \Nit entrusted me with knowledge!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.85,0:04:22.19,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What did you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.83,0:04:29.87,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What's this about a dragon's curse?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.87,0:04:31.80,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Give me more details! Right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.33,0:04:34.78,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,There's that dark, creepy hobby of yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.78,0:04:36.48,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What is this all about?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.48,0:04:38.50,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Tilty is a curse specialist.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.46,0:04:41.39,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Lady Tilty studies curses,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.39,0:04:46.43,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,meaning medical cases that can't \Nbe cured with medicine or magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.43,0:04:49.68,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I-I see... But why...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.68,0:04:53.22,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Miss Anis didn't tell you \Nabout my condition?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.22,0:04:56.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I believe she said that when you use magic, \Nyou become unbalanced,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.57,0:04:59.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,causing adverse effects \Non your mental state.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.03,0:05:00.78,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Yes, and due to that...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.28,0:05:04.60,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Well, I've made some pretty big messes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.60,0:05:09.58,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,When a noble can't even use magic right, \Nwhat else can you call it but a curse?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.87,0:05:17.07,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So that made me lose all interest in magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.55,0:05:19.97,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,and I decided to pursue medicine instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.36,0:05:26.05,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I see. Your own suffering has \Nmade you want to help others.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.05,0:05:28.13,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That's a wonderful attitude!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.09,0:05:34.55,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,There's nothing that admirable about Tilty!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.04,0:05:40.72,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,She's just a weirdo who finds \Npleasure in cracking curses!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.72,0:05:42.36,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I don't need that from a freak
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.36,0:05:45.97,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,who risks her life to study magic \Nwhen she can't even use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.79,0:05:47.44,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,And?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.12,0:05:51.66,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What does Miss Anis the Freak \Nwant me to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.12,0:06:12.93,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You're just as mad as ever, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.93,0:06:16.14,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um, would you mind showing me \Nthose papers, as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.44,0:06:19.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The knowledge I got from the dragon \Ngave me the idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.72,0:06:22.78,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I could absorb the magicite's \Npower safely this way, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.69,0:06:27.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You really intend to take \Nthis thing into yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.26,0:06:27.74,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yep!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.48,0:06:33.15,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,What are we to do with you, Princess?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.08,0:06:40.16,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Well, it sounds interesting, \Nso I'm fine with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.68,0:06:42.05,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.45,0:06:45.52,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.52,0:06:48.09,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But please, don't do anything dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.51,0:07:12.06,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Princess, you've just received \Na message from the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.09,0:07:14.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,A message?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.47,0:07:17.61,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Yes. A summons from His Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.61,0:07:19.72,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You are to visit the castle tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.31,0:07:22.17,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I-I-I didn't do anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.59,0:07:26.26,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Perhaps he caught wind of your \Nexperiments with Lady Tilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.11,0:07:30.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You think he'll be angry?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.14,0:07:32.56,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Do you think he {\i1}won't{\i0} be angry?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.56,0:07:34.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I wanna run away!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.56,0:07:37.55,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,If you do that, I believe it \Nwill only anger him more.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.69,0:07:40.08,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Good point...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.96,0:07:48.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, here I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.15,0:07:56.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I, Anisphia, have come to—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.87,0:08:03.03,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Welcome, Anisphia.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.03,0:08:06.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,M-Mother?! Why are you here?! \NYou're alive?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.39,0:08:08.96,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.67,0:08:11.92,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,And do you even need to ask why?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.92,0:08:13.76,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,With so many terrible incidents happening,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.76,0:08:16.54,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,I can't comfortably focus on diplomatic work.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.54,0:08:18.39,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,I just returned from abroad yesterday,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.39,0:08:21.86,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,and it sounds as if you've been quite active.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.86,0:08:23.95,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,After all these years,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.95,0:08:27.16,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,is it time for your mother \Nto educate you again?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.42,0:08:30.24,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,For now, just sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.24,0:08:32.45,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,O-Okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.20,0:08:41.10,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Oh, never mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.10,0:08:45.20,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,We called you here today \Nto talk about Algard.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.20,0:08:47.50,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh? About Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.50,0:08:51.83,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Yes. We've finally collated \Nall of the information.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.88,0:09:03.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hey, so Euphie really isn't to blame at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.06,0:09:06.01,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,That's true, but it's just a bit strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.77,0:09:15.95,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,All of the people who questioned Miss Cyan \Nare sympathetic toward her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.95,0:09:18.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sympathetic?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.40,0:09:24.44,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Yes. There are those who believe \Nsome of the fault lies with Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.44,0:09:27.47,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Though it clearly does not, \Nif one considers the circumstances...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.47,0:09:30.58,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,So I've decided to summon \NBaron Cyan's daughter here
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.58,0:09:33.27,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,and hear what she has to say in person.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.27,0:09:35.72,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I'd like you to be present \Nat that time. Will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.09,0:09:39.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm definitely interested, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.77,0:09:43.25,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,You may be an outlandishly wild daughter,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.25,0:09:45.64,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,but that doesn't mean we don't trust you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.07,0:09:49.43,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,With your intuition \Nand your unique point of view,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.43,0:09:51.88,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,you might notice something that we don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.34,0:09:53.61,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,We'll be counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.59,0:09:58.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.60,0:10:17.75,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So... they decided to hear \Nwhat Lady Lainie has to say,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.75,0:10:19.42,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but something seems kinda weird...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.83,0:10:22.65,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You mean how people sympathize with her?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.95,0:10:25.35,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I don't think it's that hard to believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.50,0:10:32.56,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Some stupid boys just wanted to show off \Nfor a pretty damsel in distress.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.56,0:10:34.99,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,And the head of the idiots \Nis that idiot prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.99,0:10:37.44,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hey! He's still my brother, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.25,0:10:41.66,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I mean, yeah, he {\i1}is{\i0} stupid... He is, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.66,0:10:44.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Apparently, some of the ladies \Nfeel that way, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.62,0:10:48.09,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's not just students at the academy,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.09,0:10:49.95,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but people at the castle, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.95,0:10:53.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Everyone who's talked to \NMiss Lainie is the same way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.86,0:10:54.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Isn't that crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.27,0:11:00.00,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So everyone who interacts with her \Nends up favoring her?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.48,0:11:02.97,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I might have an idea why that is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.97,0:11:06.13,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ooh! That's my dark-hearted curse nerd!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.13,0:11:07.67,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You want to be cursed to death?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.67,0:11:10.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry! I mean, great master of curses!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.21,0:11:13.11,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You're making fun of me, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.39,0:11:18.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And what is your opinion, Master Tilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.69,0:11:23.57,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Strictly speaking, it's not \Nreally a curse, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.05,0:11:36.72,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ow! Ow! That stings!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.72,0:11:39.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Do that slower! Gentler! More carefully!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.91,0:11:47.09,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,And? How did it go?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.09,0:11:52.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, well... It seems like it's \Nexactly as Tilty and I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.32,0:11:58.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Just to make sure, I talked to one of the \Npeople who was condemning Euphie,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.64,0:12:01.24,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and he had no awareness of it at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.66,0:12:06.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I just need to see Miss Lainie in person \Ntomorrow for the final confirmation.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.64,0:12:08.24,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Come with me, Ilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.24,0:12:11.65,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I haven't the slightest idea \Nwhat's going on, but very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.65,0:12:13.57,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I will entrust everything to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.57,0:12:17.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Leave it to me! I've already \Ncome up with a countermeasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.46,0:12:19.75,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,And is this your countermeasure?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.43,0:12:25.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, well... it's more like \NI figure that's how it'll turn out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.47,0:12:26.58,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.28,0:12:36.14,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I will begin making \Npreparations for tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.14,0:12:38.74,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Try not to stay in the bath too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.48,0:12:55.62,Flashback,Navre,0,0,0,,I decided to condemn her \Nat Prince Algard's suggestion.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.27,0:13:03.59,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Seriously, what the heck are you doing, Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.31,0:13:09.44,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,It suits you, Princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.08,0:13:12.03,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.03,0:13:12.89,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.38,0:13:14.34,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.00,0:13:16.18,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You look beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.18,0:13:18.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You don't have to flatter me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.89,0:13:23.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I do wish I could accompany you, \Nbut if I were there...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.57,0:13:30.41,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's okay. Just look after the place for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.81,0:13:33.70,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Okay. I'll be awaiting your return.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.70,0:13:54.14,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Baron Cyan, and his daughter, Lainie.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.14,0:13:55.73,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.73,0:14:00.89,Default,Cyan,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! Please forgive my \Ndaughter's horrendous insolence!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.24,0:14:03.40,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Be at ease, Lord Cyan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.40,0:14:07.95,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I asked you here today in hope \Nof bringing the truth to light.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.95,0:14:09.31,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Just relax for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.31,0:14:11.51,Default,Cyan,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Majesty. Please forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.51,0:14:14.13,Default,Cyan,0,0,0,,I am deeply moved by your kindness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.53,0:14:16.57,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie Cyan, raise your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.77,0:14:25.71,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,If I may be direct, you and Algard \Ndeveloped feelings for one another, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.42,0:14:30.88,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.81,0:14:34.93,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Most certainly not.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.93,0:14:38.33,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Such things are beyond my station, \Nand I have not even entertained the notion.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.94,0:14:44.05,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I would be lying if I said I did not \Nthink favorably of Prince Algard,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.05,0:14:46.31,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,but I would never dream of doing anything
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.31,0:14:49.56,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,that would cast a dark shroud \Nover the royal family's future.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.38,0:14:54.03,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I see. You certainly don't seem to be lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.11,0:14:59.24,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Indeed. There seems to be \Nno falsehood in her heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.78,0:15:02.81,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Perhaps there was some sort \Nof misunderstanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.22,0:15:07.02,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,It is possible that Algard acted hastily.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.33,0:15:10.88,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,It seems likely that there was a sad \Nmisunderstanding on both sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.32,0:15:14.59,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,It is clear that no blame \Nlies with Miss Cyan.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.59,0:15:18.26,Default,Cyan,0,0,0,,Yes! I swear to you that my \Ndaughter meant no harm!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.26,0:15:20.86,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Hmm... That seems to be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.86,0:15:22.52,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I don't feel right...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.15,0:15:40.36,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You are absolutely unbelievable!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.36,0:15:42.48,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I-It's not like that, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.48,0:15:44.96,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I, Anisphia, would like \Nto offer a suggestion!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.96,0:15:46.93,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I won't hear any excuses!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.93,0:15:48.42,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This is serious!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.56,0:15:50.89,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Speak, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.57,0:15:54.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Could you ask the others to leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.79,0:15:56.14,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.14,0:15:58.59,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,There's something I want \Nto ask Miss Lainie.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.21,0:16:03.04,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,In the interest of protecting her dignity,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.04,0:16:06.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'd like to ask it in front of \Nas few people as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.37,0:16:11.00,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,I see no problem with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.00,0:16:14.39,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I trust Anis's intuition.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.90,0:16:18.86,Default,Cyan,0,0,0,,W-Wait! My daughter really \Nisn't planning anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.26,0:16:24.33,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Princess Anisphia, don't you think \Nasking us to leave is a bit hasty?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.66,0:16:26.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Lord Chartreuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.07,0:16:31.10,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Sending everyone away so you can \Nquestion a poor, delicate young lady?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.10,0:16:34.76,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Telling her not to be afraid \Nis expecting too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.03,0:16:38.17,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I understand what you're saying,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.17,0:16:41.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but this is something that \Nnobody but me can verify.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.69,0:16:44.08,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Verify what?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.08,0:16:47.68,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Are you saying you suspect \NMiss Cyan of wrongdoing?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.68,0:16:50.31,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Do you object to what I've asked?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.77,0:16:56.32,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,The princess is clearly insisting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.32,0:16:58.78,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Should we not stand down, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.62,0:17:02.48,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I will allow it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.48,0:17:05.47,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Anis and Miss Lainie may speak in private.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.91,0:17:07.88,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,All present, leave for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.65,0:17:12.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sorry to spring this on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.32,0:17:14.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I just want to check something about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.87,0:17:17.98,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Um, I really haven't done anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.46,0:17:21.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but I need to verify this now,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.60,0:17:23.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,or you may end up at a disadvantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.74,0:17:24.99,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.72,0:17:30.74,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So the only answer you need \Nto give is "yes." Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.34,0:17:32.35,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.31,0:17:35.64,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.64,0:17:37.78,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Quiet, now. I won't do anything to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.31,0:17:39.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.48,0:17:46.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Okay, got it. All done.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.62,0:17:56.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.89,0:17:58.50,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Wh-What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.01,0:18:02.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you aware that you're using magic?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.48,0:18:03.35,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.18,0:18:07.71,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Great, so you don't realize it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.71,0:18:09.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This is a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.32,0:18:12.69,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Huh? Um, I... I'm not using any magic...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.69,0:18:16.12,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I-I don't know what you're talking about! \NI didn't do anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.12,0:18:20.31,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, I get it. I know you're \Nnot doing it of your own will.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.18,0:18:27.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie, I'm pretty sure... I think...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.68,0:18:29.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,that you're not an ordinary human.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.07,0:18:33.32,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,N-Not an ordinary... human?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.32,0:18:35.04,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Listen to me calmly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.48,0:18:38.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,There's something in your heart \Nthat I believe to be magicite.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.49,0:18:43.93,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,M-Magicite? What? But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.38,0:18:48.16,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I'm... n-not human?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.16,0:18:52.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's not that you're not human, \Nbut you're sort of like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.79,0:18:55.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I've been researching magicite,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.37,0:18:58.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and as part of that, \NI sort of took some into my body.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.63,0:19:01.66,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And that's how I can tell.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.66,0:19:06.45,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I think the magicite inside you seems to be \Na type that affects people's minds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.81,0:19:08.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,To put it more simply,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.83,0:19:12.12,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I believe you have the power of fascination.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.35,0:19:14.75,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Fascination?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.75,0:19:15.58,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yep.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.97,0:19:20.10,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Is that true?! Have I been \Ndoing that all this time?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.10,0:19:23.50,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, I don't know {\i1}that{\i0} much...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.50,0:19:25.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But I think it's highly probable.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.78,0:19:33.49,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,People have always liked me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.49,0:19:38.96,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,but that caused others to be mean to me, \Nto betray me, to bully me...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.99,0:19:45.00,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,It made me so scared, \NI started trying to avoid being liked,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.00,0:19:47.04,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,to stand out as little as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.56,0:19:56.19,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Fascination, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.19,0:20:00.01,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If not for the dragon's power, \NI would've been in trouble, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.34,0:20:06.77,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I never would have imagined there \Nwas someone with magicite in them.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.77,0:20:09.05,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,And to think it gives her the \Npower of fascination...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.38,0:20:13.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yes, but I can't say for sure \Nthat she can control that power.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.54,0:20:16.33,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's probably why it \Nactivated indiscriminately
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.33,0:20:18.13,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,against people who were kind to her,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.13,0:20:22.02,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and why she began to experience \Nfriction in her relationships.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.68,0:20:24.59,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.81,0:20:36.06,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Her power is dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.06,0:20:37.95,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,It could threaten this entire nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.42,0:20:39.67,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,We may have to...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.95,0:20:45.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,There's no problem. \NI have a countermeasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.73,0:20:50.26,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I will assume responsibility \Nand take Miss Lainie in.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.13,0:20:58.89,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Honestly... That's exactly \Nwhat's wrong with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.89,0:20:59.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.75,0:21:04.37,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Keeping Miss Lainie at your villa \Nwill cause major problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.21,0:21:06.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Problems?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.43,0:21:09.29,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Who are you living with right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.29,0:21:10.74,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.46,0:21:20.96,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Six\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}Getting to the Truth of the \NAnnulment and the Fascination
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.62,0:22:56.40,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,She is as unpredictable as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.40,0:23:00.14,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,I never expected her to get involved in this.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.14,0:23:02.10,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,This means our plan is...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.10,0:23:06.00,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,The plan remains unchanged, \Nbut we may need to move faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.91,0:23:10.58,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I should have known she would be the one \Nto stand in my way in the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.23,0:23:13.54,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,What do you intend to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.14,0:23:18.06,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,She is a problem, \Nbut she is not without flaws.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.06,0:23:19.99,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,She has plenty of weaknesses \Nwe can exploit.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.46,0:23:24.21,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Do that, then. \NMistakes will not be tolerated.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.61,0:23:27.18,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Yes, we can make no mistakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.96,0:23:31.13,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,This is the end of it, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.97,0:23:39.97,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Seven\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}The Magic Lecture of the \NFounder and the Assistant
